# Read by Cloudflare's static assets: these headers go on every file the app serves.
# (See docs/BUILD.md. The dev server does not send them.)
#
# The policy is enforced: the browser blocks anything outside it, and says so in the console
# ("Refused to ..."). To trial a change without blocking, send it as
# Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only instead, and watch the console.
#
# accounts.google.com: Google Identity Services (the sign-in script, its styles and frame).
# www.googleapis.com: the Drive API. *.googleusercontent.com: the Google account photo.
# apis.google.com, www.gstatic.com, docs.google.com: the Google Picker (folder choice for a team
# space; its page is Google's, in a frame). The Picker puts one inline <style> element on the page (the
# layout of its dialog); without it the dialog is bare text with a frame below, as first seen on the first
# real run. It is allowed by hash (style-src 'sha256-...'), not with 'unsafe-inline', so a <style> element
# of any other content is still refused. The hash is the same for every locale, device and colour scheme
# (checked 2026-11-12). If Google changes the style the dialog goes bare again: the console says
# "Applying inline style violates ... a hash ('sha256-...')" with the new one (docs/BUILD.md).
# wss://chordless.app: the live channel (docs/LIVE_SYNC.md). 'self' should cover it, but older Safari
# took 'self' to mean http(s) only; naming it costs nothing, and it is our own address.
# songselect.ccli.com: its icon in the song info dialog.
# Verovio (docs/MELODY.md), the engraver of the melody view, is WebAssembly, which needs 'wasm-unsafe-eval'. The
# page does not allow that: Verovio runs in a worker (src/js/verovio-worker.ts), and a worker has the
# policy of its own response, so the files named verovio-* (the worker and its module) get a policy of their
# own, below: scripts from here, WebAssembly, and nothing else (no network, no frames, no images). The
# `!` line takes off the page's policy first: two policies on one file are both enforced.
# style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline' allows style="" attributes only: no <style> elements.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client https://apis.google.com https://www.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style 'sha256-O5RJqRuy+/mksltO9mWs9LuNKQs/41ZS8QoMC9SP/Fg='; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' wss://chordless.app https://www.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com/gsi/ https://*.googleusercontent.com; img-src 'self' data: https://*.googleusercontent.com https://songselect.ccli.com; media-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://accounts.google.com/gsi/ https://docs.google.com https://content.googleapis.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
/assets/verovio-*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'

# Hashed files: the name changes when the content does, so they never need revalidating
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
